3. Chaos Engineering (Interview Favorite 🔥)
Definition

Controlled experiments that inject failures to build confidence in system behavior.

Principles

Define steady state (metrics)

Inject failure

Observe impact

Improve system

Kubernetes Chaos Examples

Kill random pods

Add network latency

Block DNS

Throttle CPU/memory

Real-World Example Answer

We used chaos engineering to validate our system’s behavior during pod and node failures. This helped uncover missing timeouts and misconfigured readiness probes.




